# Meridian Fracture: every platform must check out byte-identical files.
# Game data is hashed (data hash in the LAN handshake, bible mirror manifest, replay fixtures, goldens), so a CRLF
# checkout (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) would change the hash and break joins and tests.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.mfreplay binary
*.zip binary
*.dmg binary
*.deb binary
*.gz binary
*.zst binary
*.pck binary
